<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-painter-chemotactic-stripe-splitting> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Painter, Maini & Othmer (1999) chemotactic stripe splitting & stripe-spot selection (Myxococcus xanthus & Dictyostelium discoideum chemotactic cell populations)",
        "Painter, Maini & Othmer (1999) chemotactic stripe splitting & stripe-spot selection faithfully reproduces Myxococcus xanthus & Dictyostelium discoideum chemotactic cell populations morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/painter-chemotactic-stripe-splitting-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/painter-chemotactic-stripe-splitting-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/painter-chemotactic-stripe-splitting-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) 1999-painter-chemotactic-stripe-splitting.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Myxococcus xanthus & Dictyostelium discoideum chemotactic cell populations specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 91.3/100, audit 2026-10-19-chemotactic-stripe-splitting-audit-v2) and the assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/317bc3c/1999-painter-chemotactic-stripe-splitting.py> ;
    schema:about "Myxococcus xanthus & Dictyostelium discoideum chemotactic cell populations" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Individual-cell C-signal contact-reversal mechanics or 3D viscoelastic fruiting-body stalk elevation",
        "reconstructed_in_script: 1D and 2D IMEX pseudospectral Keller-Segel-Painter PDE solvers across stationary domain scales s in {1, 2, 4, 8}, subcritical chemotaxis control chi = 3.0 < chi_c = 4.5, exponentially growing domain kymograph (1 -> 2 -> 4 stripes), and 2D cubic labyrinthine stripes vs quadratic spot droplets",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Computer-vision segmentation of Myxococcus xanthus specimen (`chemotactic_pattern_specimen.jpg`, CC BY-SA 4.0) extracting 4 fruiting-body spot aggregates and 362 chemotactic rippling stripe spacings (74.10 um mean wavelength calibrated via 500 um = 125 px scale bar)",
        "reported_in_source: Keller & Segel (1970) J. Theor. Biol. 26:399-415 chemotactic flux cross-diffusion -div(n chi(c) grad(c))",
        "reported_in_source: Painter, Maini & Othmer (1999) PNAS 96(10):5549-5554 Keller-Segel chemotactic-reaction-diffusion equations, equal-diffusivity instability threshold chi > chi_c at D_n = D_c, domain-growth stripe-splitting cascade, and 2D stripe vs spot selection",
        "transfer_boundary: 1D growing domain and 2D planar chemotactic PDE mapped to Myxococcus xanthus rippling stripe ridges and fruiting-body spot aggregates" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "IV. Protista & Monera" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Slime Molds & Bacteria" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Myxococcus" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/317bc3c/1999-painter-chemotactic-stripe-splitting.py; output: docs/media/chemotactic_stripe_splitting_comparison.png; organism: Myxococcus xanthus & Dictyostelium discoideum chemotactic cell populations; checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/317bc3c; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1; spec_fingerprint: 91fb31037b136e4adc1e8bdd7b6c8097f7eaab327a03b1266cf7114f22d5f57f; artifact_sha256: c37361ad1d68ce676ba2e1cd9c205a97927c6ad87e8d8ed4de517b9bcb4418a7; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/chemotactic_stripe_splitting/chemotactic_pattern_specimen.jpg=7b1780ffcb70f313..., datasets/chemotactic_stripe_splitting/chemotactic_stripe_splitting_reference.json=2c37ed1ab3d26a08..., datasets/chemotactic_stripe_splitting/scout_manifest.json=4b4e20a991f65c81...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-chemotactic-stripe-splitting-audit; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Painter, Maini & Othmer (1999) PNAS 96(10):5549-5554 Keller-Segel chemotactic-reaction-diffusion equations, equal-diffusivity instability threshold chi > chi_c at D_n = D_c, domain-growth stripe-splitting cascade, and 2D stripe vs spot selection | Keller & Segel (1970) J. Theor. Biol. 26:399-415 chemotactic flux cross-diffusion -div(n chi(c) grad(c)); reconstructed_in_script: 1D and 2D IMEX pseudospectral Keller-Segel-Painter PDE solvers across stationary domain scales s in {1, 2, 4, 8}, subcritical chemotaxis control chi = 3.0 < chi_c = 4.5, exponentially growing domain kymograph (1 -> 2 -> 4 stripes), and 2D cubic labyrinthine stripes vs quadratic spot droplets | Computer-vision segmentation of Myxococcus xanthus specimen (`chemotactic_pattern_specimen.jpg`, CC BY-SA 4.0) extracting 4 fruiting-body spot aggregates and 362 chemotactic rippling stripe spacings (74.10 um mean wavelength calibrated via 500 um = 125 px scale bar); transfer_boundary: 1D growing domain and 2D planar chemotactic PDE mapped to Myxococcus xanthus rippling stripe ridges and fruiting-body spot aggregates; does_not_claim: Individual-cell C-signal contact-reversal mechanics or 3D viscoelastic fruiting-body stalk elevation]" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF02458621>,
